\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:11: Hooks provide an extensible event-driven system for automating actions in response to agent commands and events. Hooks are automatically discovered from directories and can be managed via CLI commands, similar to how skills work in OpenClaw.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:84: 2. **Managed hooks**: `~/.openclaw/hooks/` (user-installed, shared across workspaces)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:197: // Optionally send message to user\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:214: messages: string[],          // Push messages here to send to user\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:273: from: string,           // Sender identifier (phone number, user ID, etc.)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:287: senderUsername?: string,\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:624: - Subagent allowlist is preserved (`AGENTS.md` and `TOOLS.md` only).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:652: {\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-16T15:45:22.000Z\",\"action\":\"stop\",\"sessionKey\":\"agent:main:main\",\"senderId\":\"user@example.com\",\"source\":\"whatsapp\"}\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\hooks.md:871: User sends /new\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\troubleshooting.md:72: - Channel auth errors (`unauthorized`, `missing_scope`, `Forbidden`) �� delivery blocked by channel credentials/permissions.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\troubleshooting.md:100: openclaw config get agents.defaults.userTimezone || echo \"agents.defaults.userTimezone not set\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\troubleshooting.md:107: - `Config path not found: agents.defaults.userTimezone` means the key is unset; heartbeat falls back to host timezone (or `activeHours.timezone` if set).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\troubleshooting.md:109: - Heartbeat `activeHours` uses configured timezone resolution (`user`, `local`, or explicit IANA tz).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\automation\\webhook.md:21: // Optional: restrict explicit `agentId` routing to this allowlist.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:21: - Pairing/allowlist works the same way as other channels (`/channels/pairing` etc) with `channels.bluebubbles.allowFrom` + pairing codes.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:84: - `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.user.poke-messages.plist`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:92: <string>com.user.poke-messages</string>\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:118: - The first run may trigger macOS **Automation** prompts (`osascript` �� Messages). Approve them in the same user session that runs the LaunchAgent.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:123: launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.user.poke-messages.plist 2>/dev/null || true\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:124: launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.user.poke-messages.plist\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:140: - **DM policy**: pairing, allowlist, open, or disabled\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:162: - `channels.bluebubbles.groupPolicy = open | allowlist | disabled` (default: `allowlist`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:163: - `channels.bluebubbles.groupAllowFrom` controls who can trigger in groups when `allowlist` is set.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:179: groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:299: - `channels.bluebubbles.dmPolicy`: `pairing | allowlist | open | disabled` (default: `pairing`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:300: - `channels.bluebubbles.allowFrom`: DM allowlist (handles, emails, E.164 numbers, `chat_id:*`, `chat_guid:*`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:301: - `channels.bluebubbles.groupPolicy`: `open | allowlist | disabled` (default: `allowlist`).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:302: - `channels.bluebubbles.groupAllowFrom`: Group sender allowlist.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:309: - `channels.bluebubbles.mediaLocalRoots`: Explicit allowlist of absolute local directories permitted for outbound local media paths. Local path sends are denied by default unless this is configured. Per-account override: `channels.bluebubbles.accounts.<accountId>.mediaLocalRoots`.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\bluebubbles.md:327: - Direct handles: `+15555550123`, `user@example.com`\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:21: Broadcast groups are evaluated after channel allowlists and group activation rules. In WhatsApp groups, this means broadcasts happen when OpenClaw would normally reply (for example: on mention, depending on your group settings).\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:166: Note: broadcast groups do not bypass channel allowlists or group activation rules (mentions/commands/etc). They only change _which agents run_ when a message is eligible for processing.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:184: - Different skills installed\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:194: History: [user message, alfred's previous responses]\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:195: Workspace: /Users/pascal/openclaw-alfred/\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:203: History: [user message, baerbel's previous responses]\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:204: Workspace: /Users/pascal/openclaw-baerbel/\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\broadcast-groups.md:375: **User sends:** Code snippet\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:2: summary: \"Discord bot support status, capabilities, and configuration\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:32: Click **Bot** on the sidebar. Set the **Username** to whatever you call your OpenClaw agent.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:40: - **Server Members Intent** (recommended; required for role allowlists and name-to-ID matching)\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:57: Click **OAuth2** on the sidebar. You'll generate an invite URL with the right permissions to add the bot to your server.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:64: A **Bot Permissions** section will appear below. Enable:\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:80: 1. Click **User Settings** (gear icon next to your avatar) �� **Advanced** �� toggle on **Developer Mode**\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:82: 3. Right-click your **own avatar** �� **Copy User ID**\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:84: Save your **Server ID** and **User ID** alongside your Bot Token �� you'll send all three to OpenClaw in the next step.\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:114: > \"I already set my Discord bot token in config. Please finish Discord setup with User ID `<user_id>` and Server ID `<server_id>`.\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:176: <Step title=\"Add your server to the guild allowlist\">\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:181: > \"Add my Discord Server ID `<server_id>` to the guild allowlist\"\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:189: groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:193: users: [\"YOUR_USER_ID\"],\r\nC:\\Users\\���\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\openclaw\\docs\\channels\\discord.md:243: If you need shared context in every channel, put the stable instructions in `AGENTS.md` or `USER.md` (they are injected for every session). Keep long-term notes in `MEMORY.md` and access them on demand with memory tools.\r